      "writtenOn": "2023-07-26T20:37:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Normally functionality that needs to know the lifecycle state should be implemented by subscribing to Application.ActivityLifecycleCallbacks. This would also ensure that the developers implement the necessary state change handling.\n\nWhat is the reason why it can\u0027t be used?",
      "revId": "1250f17dffab41880b2f7c4b78d9754a83dab84a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2f3c4234_fbc38400",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074459
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-26T20:39:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "NFC stack has a bunch of these usages which were added maybe before ActivityLifeCycleCallbacks.\n\nBut, even with ActivityLifeCycleCallbacks, we do use isResumed() to get the current state when the app registers an activity for NFC operation (See [here](https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/base/core/java/android/nfc/NfcActivityManager.java;l\u003d121?q\u003dNfcActivityManage\u0026sq\u003drepo:googleplex-android%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain%20b:main))",
      "parentUuid": "021a9509_6e05be73",
      "revId": "1250f17dffab41880b2f7c4b78d9754a83dab84a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "67b5c58e_1d652907",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1097438
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-26T20:49:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Normally one should register the callback and cache the last observed state, which can be used to implement `isResumed` locally.\n\nMy understanding is that normally usage of existing APIs is preferred to adding new ones to the surface, so I\u0027m wondering if there is some blocker here.",
      "parentUuid": "2f3c4234_fbc38400",
      "revId": "1250f17dffab41880b2f7c4b78d9754a83dab84a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "520f3ea4_86ae10cd",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074459
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-26T20:55:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Normally one should register the callback and cache the last observed state, which can be used to implement isResumed locally.\n\nYeah, that is what the class `NfcActivityManager.java` tries to do. But, how do we get the current state before we get some state transition callback? should we just assume that it is resumed?",
      "parentUuid": "67b5c58e_1d652907",
      "revId": "1250f17dffab41880b2f7c4b78d9754a83dab84a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a25a4012_fe32c4b1",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1097438
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-27T02:31:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could you point me to how `NfcActivityState` / `NfcActivityManager` is used - can\u0027t find it in code. Can the lifecycle callback be registered in `Application#onCreate`, before any activities are live?",
      "parentUuid": "520f3ea4_86ae10cd",
      "revId": "1250f17dffab41880b2f7c4b78d9754a83dab84a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0d45ae55_2fafba3a",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074459
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-27T17:07:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Usage is [here](https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/base/core/java/android/nfc/NfcAdapter.java;l\u003d1542?q\u003dNfcActivityManager\u0026sq\u003drepo:googleplex-android%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain%20b:main). The NFC API accepts an activity from the app and we change NFC state based on the request. when the activity goes to paused state (i.e !isResumed()), we restore state back to what it was before the app request.\n\n\u003e can\u0027t find it in code. Can the lifecycle callback be registered in Application#onCreate, before any activities are live?\n\nSince the activity is provided by the app to the NFC stack, there is no guarantee that the activity is not created at that point of time.",
      "parentUuid": "a25a4012_fe32c4b1",
      "revId": "1250f17dffab41880b2f7c4b78d9754a83dab84a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3baea496_48a64f07",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1097438
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-27T20:49:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@ilake@google.com @diegovela@google.com @louischang@google.com I imagine that `Application.ActivityLifecycleCallbacks` not returning the current state upon registration might be a common inconvenience for libraries that need to know the current state (assuming the app doesn\u0027t use any AndroidX wrappers or initializers). \n\nDo you have any recommendations? Should we consider a version of the lifecycle callback API in the platform that would immediately report the current state upon registration? Or a direct way to synchronously get the current Activity state similar to `LifecycleOwner` / `Lifecycle`?",
      "parentUuid": "0d45ae55_2fafba3a",
      "revId": "1250f17dffab41880b2f7c4b78d9754a83dab84a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bb6dd1a0_ae55db2d",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1650201
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-28T17:02:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Some thoughts.\n1) We should immediately report the current state upon registration.  There might be a subtlety like what state are you in if you are in the \"onCreate\" method.  \n\n2) As for a synchronous method, I would generally advise against this initially since synchronous reads on mutable data are error prone.  If we did provide it, we should probably guard it by checking the read is on the main thread.",
      "parentUuid": "3baea496_48a64f07",
      "revId": "1250f17dffab41880b2f7c4b78d9754a83dab84a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
